# Brooch Identity domain rules

## Auth model
- Cookie session `brooch_sid` (HttpOnly) — SPA never reads it
- CSRF: `GET /api/v1/auth/csrf` returns raw `{ token }` (not ApiResponse); send `X-XSRF-TOKEN` on unsafe non-exempt POSTs
- CSRF-exempt: login, set-password, forgot-password(+complete), login-intent, csrf, tenants/register
- Every authenticated call: `X-Brooch-Application: identity` + `Accept-Language`
- Interceptor order: **application header → language → csrf → error**

## Login decision tree (exact order)
1. `requiresTenantSelection === true` → `/select-company` (wins even if redirectUrl set)
2. Navigable `redirectUrl` → full-page `location.assign` (not Angular router cross-origin)
3. Else → stay in Identity, `GET /auth/me`, applications launcher

## Selection stage
- Picker rows ONLY from `LoginResponse.availableCompanies` — never rebuild from `/me/companies`
- Keep `intentId` in AuthFlowStore across selection (API does not echo it)
- Selection allow-list only; other APIs → 401 Auth.NotAuthenticated (route to picker, not login)

## SSO / redirects
- Sibling apps hand off via opaque `?intentId=` only
- Trust only backend `redirectUrl` or registry `baseUrl` (absolute http/https)
- Same-app `returnUrl` must be relative starting with single `/`
- App switch = navigate to `baseUrl` — no backend select-application endpoint
- Workspace logout = `POST /auth/logout-all`

## Authz
- Permissions gate **actions/nav links**, never routes — backend 403 is truth
- `/roles` is read-only viewer in v1
- Coded 401 = business denial (stay); uncoded 401 = session loss → re-auth
- `login-intent` may return HTTP 200 with `isValid: false` — treat as failure

## Registration
- `POST /tenants/register` — no password; then set-password email → login
- No OTP — 4-digit set-password codes / reset tokens only

## API
- Features call `*Api` services only — never invent endpoints
- Dev SPA: `https://dev.account.brooch.sa:4300` (ssl + host); `apiBaseUrl` absolute to staging (`https://stg.api.brooch.sa/api/v1`)
- No local API proxy — backend must CORS-allow the Identity origin (same pattern as CRM)

## Errors
- HTTP errors are global — see `.cursor/rules/error-handling.mdc` (interceptor + banner; no component error UI)
